Gyneconomy is the reading companion to the book "Mrs. Market". Its source is public
so that the app can be hosted, read and audited — not as a grant of licence.

You MAY:
  - read this source, and study how it works;
  - run it locally for your own private use;
  - quote short excerpts with attribution, as you would quote any published work;
  - open issues and propose changes.

You MAY NOT, without written permission:
  - copy, redistribute or host this work or a substantial part of it;
  - make derivative works, including reskins, translations and ports;
  - use the design, the writing, the season framework or the indicator model in
    another product;
  - use the name "Gyneconomy" or "Mrs. Market".

The economic data this app displays is not covered by this notice. It belongs to the
agencies and index originators that publish it — the U.S. Treasury, the Federal
Reserve and its regional banks, the Bureau of Labor Statistics, the Bureau of
Economic Analysis, the Congressional Budget Office, the OECD, Eurostat, the World
Bank, ICE Data Indices, S&P Dow Jones Indices, ISM, Cboe, Robert Shiller and CNN.
Each figure names its source on the app's Sources screen. Their terms govern their
data, not this notice.

Nothing here is investment advice.

